From 100a52a3ba5945999d5faaff871714967c9eb30e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:56:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the Funnel Audit page: master-detail layout,
 verdict-first hierarchy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the highest-impact items from the earlier 15-point review —
the goal was a real information hierarchy instead of one long column of
identically-styled sections.

leak-map-schedule.tsx:
- "Next weekly/monthly audit" collapsed from two hero tiles into one
  compact metadata line — it's checked once, doesn't need that much
  vertical weight.
- Real master-detail layout: a narrow, sticky timeline rail on the left
  (own internal scroll) and the selected audit's full detail on the
  right, side by side on wide screens instead of stacked (which
  guaranteed the actual diagnostic content was always below the fold).
  Stacks back to one column on mobile.
- Timeline rows simplified for the narrower rail — dropped the
  SquishySkillBadge (redundant, the whole page is this one skill) and
  the boxed Automated/Manual pill (now a small icon only when manual).
- Removed the right column's own severity pill + Issues/Alerts/Gaps
  3-tile grid — it duplicated exactly what the embedded LeakMapView
  already shows, just less completely. Right column now only supplies
  audit type + timestamp + "open full page", and lets the embedded
  view own the actual verdict.

leak-map-view.tsx (shared by both the schedule's embedded panel and the
standalone run page):
- Verdict banner is now the first, biggest thing on the page — bigger
  dot, bigger text, more padding — since "is anything wrong" is the
  answer this view exists to give, not a footnote under a timeline.
- Issues split into "Needs attention" (real high/medium findings, full
  visual weight) vs. everything else (healthy or insufficient-data,
  muted, collapsed behind a <details> disclosure whenever there's a
  real finding to prioritize over instead of competing with it).
- Data Gaps folded into its own <details> disclosure instead of a
  permanent sticky sidebar duplicating the same insufficient-data
  metrics already listed above.
- Per-metric Current/Prior/Shift collapsed from a 3-column stat grid
  into one compact line.
- Executive Report no longer forced into a max-h-80 overflow-y-auto
  box — it flows in the page's own scroll like the rest of the content,
  instead of being hidden behind an undiscoverable inner scrollbar.

